From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: imx8-mipi-csi2-sam: don't warn about missing sensor
 during PHY reset

mipi_csis_imx8mp_phy_reset() calls csis_get_remote_subdev(), which
unconditionally logs "No remote pad found!" / "No remote subdev
found!" whenever the sensor isn't bound yet.

mipi_csis_probe() calls mipi_csis_imx8mp_phy_reset() before
mipi_csis_subdev_init()/media_entity_pads_init() run, so the CSIS
entity has zero pads at that point and the sensor can never be found.
mipi_csis_imx8mp_phy_reset() already handles this gracefully (it falls
back to a default RAW12 configuration via csi_phy_initial_cfg), so
this is not an error condition, yet it always prints:

  mipi_csis_imx8mp_phy_reset, No remote pad found!

on every boot, regardless of whether the sensor is present, wired, or
working correctly, which is misleading.

Look up the remote subdev directly with csis_get_remote_sensor_pad()
and media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev() instead of via the logging wrapper
csis_get_remote_subdev(), since a missing sensor is an expected,
already-handled case here. The other call sites of
csis_get_remote_subdev() (mipi_csis_s_power(), mipi_csis_set_fmt(),
etc.) are left unchanged, since a missing sensor there does indicate a
real problem.

Signed-off-by: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate NXP proprietary driver
---
 drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-mipi-csi2-sam.c | 13 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-mipi-csi2-sam.c b/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-mipi-csi2-sam.c
index 05e081e47b13..65ff1667bb08 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-mipi-csi2-sam.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-mipi-csi2-sam.c
@@ -1723,6 +1723,7 @@ static void mipi_csis_imx8mp_phy_reset(struct csi_state *state)
 {
 	int ret = 0;
 	struct v4l2_subdev *sen_sd;
+	struct media_pad *source_pad;
 	struct reset_control *reset = state->mipi_reset;
 
 	struct v4l2_subdev_mbus_code_enum code = {
@@ -1735,7 +1736,17 @@ static void mipi_csis_imx8mp_phy_reset(struct csi_state *state)
 	reset_control_deassert(reset);
 	usleep_range(10, 20);
 
-	sen_sd = csis_get_remote_subdev(state, __func__);
+	/*
+	 * The sensor may legitimately not be bound yet at this point (e.g.
+	 * during initial probe(), before the media pads even exist), so
+	 * look up the remote subdev directly instead of via
+	 * csis_get_remote_subdev() to avoid its "No remote pad/subdev
+	 * found!" error log, which would be misleading here: this reset
+	 * only uses the sensor's format as an optional hint and already
+	 * falls back to a sane default when it is absent.
+	 */
+	source_pad = csis_get_remote_sensor_pad(state);
+	sen_sd = source_pad ? media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(source_pad->entity) : NULL;
 	if (!sen_sd)
 		goto csi_phy_initial_cfg;
 
-- 
